{
  section === "method" &&
    (zh ? (
      <>
        <h3>需求：岗位</h3>
        <p>
          {longDate(lang, snapshot)} Metix AI Platform 上的在招岗位，职位描述里提到某个工具。Claude Code、GitHub Copilot、LangChain、LangGraph、LlamaIndex、CrewAI、AutoGen、DSPy
          和 Model Context Protocol 按名称匹配；Cursor、Codex、Windsurf 需要同一段描述里还提到另一个 AI 编程工具。定义在{" "}
          <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/cases/${entry.slug}/queries/tools.json`}>tools.json</a>。
        </p>
        <h3>供给：档案</h3>
        <p>
          在技能栏里列出同一个工具的个人档案，条件和岗位一一对应。只做计数，没有读取任何档案，也没有读取任何岗位。所有人数都经过小格子规则：少于 10 的写成 "&lt;10"。
        </p>
        <h3>抽检</h3>
        <p>
          agent 读了职位描述样本来检查匹配：Claude Code 和 GitHub Copilot 40 条里 40 条是工具本身，AutoGen 40 条里 39 条。只看单词时 Cursor、Codex、Windsurf
          分别是 60 条里 55、55、56 条，所以收紧了条件；收紧后这三个工具在档案里只剩 258、452、13 人，比值没有意义，因此不参与供需比较。
        </p>
        <h3>国家、行业和薪资</h3>
        <p>
          国家是至少提到一个编程助手的岗位按 location.country 计数，其余国家合并。行业是挑选出的列表，不是排名，一个岗位可以属于多个行业。薪资对照组是标题含 "software
          engineer" 的美国岗位，两组可能重叠。维度定义在 <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/cases/${entry.slug}/queries/dimensions.json`}>dimensions.json</a>。
        </p>
        <h3>局限</h3>
        <p>
          档案的技能栏由本人填写、更新慢，越新的工具越可能被低估，所以比值衡量的是需求和已公开技能之间的差距。岗位的重复发布没有合并。提到一个工具不等于要求会用它。这是快照当天的截面。
        </p>
      </>
    ) : (
      <>
        <h3>Demand: postings</h3>
        <p>
          Open postings on the Metix AI Platform on {longDate(lang, snapshot)} whose description names a tool. Claude Code, GitHub
          Copilot, LangChain, LangGraph, LlamaIndex, CrewAI, AutoGen, DSPy, and the Model Context Protocol match by name; Cursor,
          Codex, and Windsurf count only when the description names another AI coding tool as well. The definitions are in{" "}
          <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/cases/${entry.slug}/queries/tools.json`}>tools.json</a>.
        </p>
        <h3>Supply: profiles</h3>
        <p>
          Profiles that list the same tool among their skills, with conditions that mirror the postings. Everything is a count: no
          profile and no posting is read. Every count of people passes the small-cell rule, so anything under 10 shows as "&lt;10".
        </p>
        <h3>Audit</h3>
        <p>
          The agent read samples of job descriptions to check the matches. Claude Code and GitHub Copilot meant the tool in 40 of
          40, AutoGen in 39 of 40. The plain words held in 55, 55, and 56 of 60 for Cursor, Codex, and Windsurf, so their
          condition was tightened. Tightened, those three leave only 258, 452, and 13 profiles, too few for a meaningful ratio, so
          they stay out of the demand and supply comparison.
        </p>
        <h3>Countries, industries, and pay</h3>
        <p>
          Countries count postings that name at least one assistant by location.country, with the rest combined. Industries are
          a selected list, not a ranking, and a posting can list several. The pay comparison uses US postings titled "software
          engineer", which can overlap with the first group. The dimensions are in{" "}
          <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/cases/${entry.slug}/queries/dimensions.json`}>dimensions.json</a>.
        </p>
        <h3>Limits</h3>
        <p>
          Skills on a profile are self-reported and updated slowly, and newer tools are the most likely to be missing, so the
          ratios measure the gap between demand and published skills. Reposts are not collapsed. Naming a tool is not the same as
          requiring it. This is one day, not a trend.
        </p>
      </>
    ))
}

